 p. 142); Art. 24, Convention Cour des Prises 1907.","en":"New; cf. Art. 23, Draft Convention, 1907; Art. 7, Hague Project, Annex 2, 1910 (Une Cour de Justice Internationale, p. 142); Art. 24, Prize Court Convention, 1907.","full_text":""},"speaker":null,"sources":["Edition"],"evidence":[{"concept":"c.root-phillimore-plan-article-24","weight":1.0,"end":144,"label":"Art. 24","lang":"fr","start":137},{"concept":"c.root-phillimore-plan-article-24","weight":1.0,"end":132,"label":"Art. 24","lang":"en","start":125}]}]},{"meeting":22,"section":"22","passages":[{"seg_id":"s0505.06","meeting":22,"doc":"minutes","pdf":505,"printed":495,"texts":{"fr":"Le PRESIDENT, ouvrant la discussion sur l'article 24 du projet Root—Phillimore, soulève la question de savoir s'il ne faut pas indiquer que la Cour aura la faculté de siéger ailleurs. Il attire l'attention sur la formule insérée dans l'article 13 de son avant-projet.","en":"The PRESIDENT, in laying Article 24 of the Root—Phillimore plan before the Committee, raised the question as to whether a provision should not be included giving the Court the right to sit elsewhere. He drew attention to the clause contained in Article 13 of his plan.","full_text":""},"speaker":{"seg_id":"s0505.06","speaker_id":"descamps","certain":true,"name":"Baron Édouard Descamps","role":"member"},"sources":["Edition"],"evidence":[{"concept":"c.root-phillimore-plan-article-24","weight":1.0,"end":78,"file":"all.p1.jsonl","lang":"fr","line":3939,"start":40}]},{"seg_id":"s0506.03","meeting":22,"doc":"minutes","pdf":506,"printed":496,"texts":{"fr":"M. DE LAPRADELLE fait valoir que cet argument parle en faveur de l'adoption de la formule simple qui se trouve à l'article 24 du projet Root—Phillimore.","en":"M. DE LAPRADELLE pointed out that this argument was in favour of the adoption of the simple wording contained in Article 24 of the Root—Phillimore plan.","full_text":""},"speaker":{"seg_id":"s0506.03","speaker_id":"lapradelle","certain":true,"name":"Albert de